'''''Moraea sisyrinchium''''', commonly the '''Barbary nut''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] that belongs to the tribe [[Irideae]]. It is native to southern [[Europe]] and the [[Mediterranean basin|Mediterranean region]].<ref name="PBS">{{cite web|url=http://pacificbulbsociety.org/pbswiki/index.php/Gynandriris|title=Gynandriris|publisher=Pacific Bulb Society|accessdate=23 April 2017}}</ref><ref name="FoI">{{cite web|url=http://www.flowersinisrael.com/Gynandririssisyrinchium_page.htm|title=Moraea sisyrinchium|work=Flowers of Israel|accessdate=23 April 2017}}</ref><ref name="GF">{{cite web|url=http://www.greekflora.gr/el/flowers/0292/Moraea-sisyrinchium|title=greek flora|accessdate=23 April 2017}}</ref>

